[[File:BotW North Gate.png|thumb|right|320px|The North Gate of Gerudo Town]]
Gerudo Town is the primary settlement of the [[Gerudo Desert]], and it consequently serves as the home of the [[Gerudo]] people. Since the Gerudo are a solely female race, they only allow women to enter the Town.<ref>{{Cite|They {{Color BotW|Red|only let women into that town}}...And to think we came all the way out here...|Robsten|BotW}}</ref> When inside Gerudo Town, [[Link]] will not be subjected to the [[Heat]] or [[Freezing Climate]] of the Gerudo Desert. The [[Daqo Chisay Shrine]] resides right outside Gerudo Town's walls. Gerudo Town also houses a [[Goddess Statue]] near the [[Southeast Gate]], where Link can exchange [[Spirit Orb]]s for [[Heart Container]]s or [[Stamina Vessel]]s.<ref>{{Cite|It appears you have claimed {{Color BotW|Red|four}} {{Color BotW|Blue|Spirit Orbs}}. In exchange for {{Color BotW|Red|four}} {{Color BotW|Blue|Spirit Orbs}}, I will amplify your being. So tell me what it is that you desire.|Goddess Statue|BotW}}</ref>

In the past, Gerudo Town was constructed around the largest oasis in the Gerudo Desert.<ref name="CaC 315">{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 315}}</ref> The Town's [[Water (Terrain)|Water]] is sourced from the [[Royal Palace]], where it then flows throughout the town within waterways.<ref name="CaC 316">{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 316}}</ref> Being isolated from the rest of [[Hyrule]], Gerudo Town's culture developed independently and is considered to be unique.<ref name="CaC 315"/> During the [[Great Calamity]] 100 years prior to the events of {{BotW}}, Gerudo Town was spared any damage from the [[Guardian]]s' assault, though their chief at the time, [[Urbosa]], was killed while fighting [[Thunderblight Ganon]].<ref>{{Cite|Stay on your edge, Link! This formidable adversary was made by Ganon and brought me to a warrior's demise 100 years ago.|Urbosa|BotW}}</ref> In modern times, the chief of Gerudo Town is [[Riju]], who inherited the position at a young age due to her mother's untimely demise.<ref>{{Cite|Buliara told me today that Mother has passed on and gone to a better place... She said that my mother's death means I am now the chief of the Gerudo people. I wish she'd stayed here, though. I don't see how it can be a better place with us apart...|Chief's Diary|BotW}}</ref> When [[Divine Beast Vah Naboris]] became active in the [[East Barrens]], the Gerudo began to fear that it would trample their Town.<ref>{{Cite|That's the {{Color BotW|Blue|Divine Beast Vah Naboris}}. They say it used to be a god who protected this area, but... It suddenly appeared a little while ago and just started walking around aimlessly. Everyone's afraid that it may wander into town eventually.|Lashley|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Having investigated Divine Vah Naboris, I can say that if it came to Gerudo Town, we'd be helpless.|Chief's Diary|BotW}}</ref>

When Link normally tries to enter Gerudo Town, he will be stopped by the guards.<ref>{{Cite|Freeze! Where do you think you're going?! Not into town—that's for sure! No voe allowed. Off with you!|Dorrah|BotW}}</ref> As part of the "[[Forbidden City Entry]]" [[Main Quest]], Link is tasked with finding a man who was supposedly able to enter Gerudo Town.<ref>{{Cite|You heard of a man at the Kara Kara Bazaar who found a way to sneak into Gerudo Town, a place men are forbidden from entering.<br/><br/>Try and locate some people who know his whereabouts.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref> After receiving the [[Gerudo Outfit]] from [[Vilia]], Link will be able to pass through the gates of Gerudo Town.<ref>{{Cite|You snuck into Gerudo Town successfully!<br/><br/>You were able to fool the town guards by disguising yourself in a Gerudo outfit.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref> In addition to other pieces of the Gerudo Outfit, Link can wear the [[Sand Boots]], the [[Snow Boots]], and the [[Thunder Helm]] in Gerudo Town without being thrown out by the guards.

During the "[[Divine Beast Vah Naboris (Quest)|Divine Beast Vah Naboris]]" [[Main Quest]], Link offers Riju and [[Buliara]] his help in calming the [[Divine Beast]].<ref>{{Cite|[I can calm Naboris.] You think you have what it takes to subdue something so powerful as a Divine Beast? The only ones who could ever control them were Champions like Lady Urbosa. And all the Champions died in the {{Color BotW|Red|Calamity}} 100 years ago.|Buliara|BotW}}</ref> Before he can do so, he must first prove himself by retrieving the Thunder Helm, which was stolen by the [[Yiga|Yiga Clan]].<ref>{{Cite|Lady Riju! I don't see how you can trust a complete stranger with something as important as this task. Perhaps if this person were first to prove his worth by recovering your stolen Thunder Helm...|Buliara|BotW}}</ref> Once he returns to Gerudo Town with the Thunder Helm, he will be directed to meet with Riju outside of her [[Riju's Bedroom|Bedroom]], which is located on the second floor of the Royal Palace.<ref>{{Cite|If you are looking for {{Color BotW|Blue|Lady Riju}}, she's on the {{Color BotW|Red|second floor}}. Normally people aren't allowed into her sleeping quarters, but she has given you special permission it seems...|Buliara|BotW}}</ref> There, she tells him to meet her at the [[Lookout Post]] when he is ready to face Divine Beast Vah Naboris.<ref>{{Cite|I'll head out now. Let's meet up at the {{Color BotW|Red|lookout post}} {{Color BotW|Blue|south of town}}.|Riju|BotW}}</ref> After Link successfully appeases the Divine Beast, Riju will allow him to take the [[Scimitar of the Seven]] and the [[Daybreaker]] as a reward for saving Gerudo Town.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Blue|Naboris}} is no longer a threat to the town... I'm still worried about the larger threat to Hyrule, but at least my people won't be troubled by {{Color BotW|Blue|Naboris}} anymore. I want to offer you these as thanks for your help. I trust you'll accept them. These pieces of equipment are priceless treasures of the Gerudo people. They were once worn by {{Color BotW|Blue|Lady Urbosa}}. Since you and {{Color BotW|Blue|Lady Urbosa}} were friends, it's only right that you have them.|Riju|BotW}}</ref>

Initially, a total of three [[Side Quest]]s can be found in Gerudo Town, those being "[[Medicinal Molduga]]",<ref>{{Cite|Malena's husband has fallen ill. He needs the {{Color BotW|Red|guts of a Molduga}} in order to get better. The Molduga is a ferocious monster that's sensitive to the slightest vibration, and it attacks anything that comes near it. The woman is desperately looking for help, but nobody seems capable...|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref> "[[The Secret Club's Secret]]",<ref>{{Cite|The clothes shop Fashion Passion has a secret entrance where only members can get in. To gain entrance, you need a {{Color BotW|Red|secret password}} known only to members. It seems that once you give the wrong password, you won't be able to try again for an entire day.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref> and "[[Tools of the Trade]]".<ref>{{Cite|Isha, the jeweler, is in a bind. She ran out of the flint she needs to keep making her accessories. She says that she can reopen her store if you bring her {{Color BotW|Red|10 pieces of flint}}.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref> "[[The Seven Heroines]]" [[Shrine Quest]] can also be obtained after Link is able to enter Gerudo Town.<ref>{{Cite|There are statues of {{Color BotW|Red|the seven heroines}} east of Gerudo Town. They may have something to do with the location of a hidden shrine.<br/><br/>First, solve the meaning behind the message: "When the symbols of the seven find their place, the blessed path will be revealed."|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref> After the "Divine Beast Vah Naboris" Main Quest has been completed, three new Side Quests become available, which are "[[The Mystery Polluter]]",<ref>{{Cite|Dalia has been working hard to start an orchard, but garbage keeps appearing in her water source, so her efforts are all for naught. What sort of {{Color BotW|Red|vile polluter}} would toss his or her garbage away with such indifference?|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref> "[[The Search for Barta]]",<ref>{{Cite|Barta has disappeared again. She headed south in search of {{Color BotW|Red|leviathan bones}} but never came back. Not only is the area home to Molduga, but it's also known for {{Color BotW|Red|extreme heat}}. You'll need special gear, or you'll be in danger. Use your map to search for Barta.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref> and "[[The Thunder Helm]]".<ref>{{Cite|The Thunder Helm has been passed down as a prized treasure of the Gerudo since Urbosa's time. It doesn't seem like they'll just give it to you, but if you're able to {{Color BotW|Red|solve all}} the town's problems, they'll at least lend it to you.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref>

Two separate [[Treasure Chest]]s are located within Gerudo Town. The first is a wooden Chest can be found in the storage area northeast of [[Fashion Passion]], and it contains a [[Silver Rupee]]. A second Treasure Chest made of metal is buried in the [[Sand]] near the Southeast Gate, which Link can find a [[Golden Bow]] inside of.

